  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers and clients pay for skill and reliability, not for the source of your plan. They judge you by evidence, so free guidance should lead to a trial and a sample.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is checking who runs a service and what it does with your data.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and judging free online career guidance: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools suggest careers from interests and summarise roles. Treat the output as a list to test, not an answer.
  </p>
  <p>
    Self-knowledge, real trials and decisions you own hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to generate options; later, test them with people and small projects.
  </p>

  <h2 id="better">Alternatives that can beat a general judging free online career guidance path</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Alternative</th>
          <th>Why it can beat it</th>
          <th>Catch</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
