  <h2 id="learn">How to learn judging free online career guidance cheaply, and what proof counts</h2>

  <p>
    Judging free online career guidance is learned by doing real work, so the cheapest route is also the best. A paid course is worth it only when it gives feedback and finished work that you cannot get free.
  </p>
  <h3>Free and low-cost routes first</h3>
  <ul class="check-list">
    <li>Free worksheets and public notices.</li>
    <li>Free talks with seniors.</li>
    <li>Free day-in-the-life videos.</li>
    <li>A teacher who knows you.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>How to judge a paid course</h3>
  <p>
    Judge each course, not the platform. Ask what you will build, who reviews it, which role graduates reached, how current the material is and what the refund terms are, in writing.
  </p>
  <h3>Your week, and a first small test</h3>
  <p>
    A starting plan is about ten hours a week: three of lessons and seven of practice on one project. Do not pay for an expensive programme before this habit holds.
  </p>
  <p>
    This week, use two free sources, compare their lists and write a shortlist of two options.
  </p>
  <h3>Building a high-income skill portfolio beside the credential</h3>
  <p>
    A degree has a place, and the weak spot is relying on it alone. A skill mix of one core skill, a second skill, communication, a niche and a clear offer builds a high-income skill portfolio, and a niche service can bring an earlier financial freedom.
  </p>

  <h2 id="check">A trust checklist for free guidance</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Check</th>
          <th>Good sign</th>
          <th>Warning sign</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Check"><strong>Who runs it</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Good sign">Named people or institution with a track record</td>
          <td data-label="Warning sign">No names or contact details</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Check"><strong>Your data</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Good sign">Clear statement of use and no sale of contact details</td>
          <td data-label="Warning sign">Asks for many details before showing anything</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Check"><strong>Advice style</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Good sign">Asks about you and gives options</td>
          <td data-label="Warning sign">Pushes one product</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Check"><strong>Follow-up</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Good sign">Optional and clearly marked</td>
          <td data-label="Warning sign">Repeated pressure calls or messages</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Check"><strong>Claims</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Good sign">Honest about limits</td>
          <td data-label="Warning sign">Guaranteed outcomes</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

